rst line of each test case contains one integer `n`\n(`1 <= n <= 2 * 10^5`), the length of `p`.\n\nThe second line of each test case contains `n` integers\n`p_1, p_2, ..., p_n` (`1 <= p_i <= n`, all `p_i` are distinct), the elements\nof `p`.\n\nIt is guaranteed that the sum of `n` over all test cases does not exceed\n`2 * 10^5`.\n\n## Output\n\nFor each test case, print one integer, the number of good starting positions.\n\n## Example\n\n### Input\n\n```text\n4\n1\n1\n5\n1 3 5 2 4\n6\n1 2 4 5 3 6\n7\n1 3 5 7 2 4 6\n```\n\n### Output\n\n```text\n1\n4\n3\n0\n```\n\n## Note\n\nIn the first test case, there is only one starting position. Every non-empty\nprefix contains the single value `1`, so it has one block. Thus, this position\nis good.\n\nIn the second test case, after reading the first `3` numbers from position `1`,\nthe set is `{1, 3, 5}` and has `3` blocks. Thus, position `1` is not good. Each\nof the other `4` positions is good.","type":"text"}],"contestId":2250,"index":"E","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Double-Rift Dial","problemKey":"2250-E","rating":null,"tags":["data structures","dfs and similar","dsu","implementation","two pointers"],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2250/problem/E"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int testCases;\n    cin >> testCases;\n\n    while (testCases--) {\n        int n;\n        int targetXor;\n        cin >> n >> targetXor;\n\n        const bool isPowerOfTwo = (n & (n - 1)) == 0;\n        if (!isPowerOfTwo || (n == 2 && targetXor != 0)) {\n            cout << -1 << '\\n';\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        if (targetXor == 0) {\n            for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n                for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n                    if (column > 0) {\n                        cout << ' ';\n                    }\n                    cout << (row ^ column);\n                }\n                cout << '\\n';\n            }\n            continue;\n        }\n\n        vector<char> visited(n, false);\n        vector<int> evenPositionValues;\n        vector<int> oddPositionValues;\n        evenPositionValues.reserve(n / 2);\n        oddPositionValues.reserve(n / 2);\n\n        int pairIndex = 0;\n        for (int value = 0; value < n; ++value) {\n            if (visited[value]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            const int partner = value ^ targetXor;\n            visited[value] = true;\n            visited[partner] = true;\n\n            vector<int>& destination =\n                pairIndex < n / 4 ? oddPositionValues : evenPositionValues;\n            destination.push_back(value);\n            destination.push_back(partner);\n            ++pairIndex;\n        }\n\n        vector<int> ordering(n);\n        int evenIndex = 0;\n        int oddIndex = 0;\n        for (int index = 0; index < n; ++index) {\n            if (index % 2 == 0) {\n                ordering[index] = evenPositionValues[evenIndex++];\n            } else {\n                ordering[index] = oddPositionValues[oddIndex++];\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n            for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n                int value = ordering[row] ^ ordering[column];\n                if (row % 2 == 1 && column % 2 == 1) {\n                    value ^= targetXor;\n                }\n\n                if (column > 0) {\n                    cout << ' ';\n                }\n                cout << value;\n            }\n            cout << '\\n';\n        }\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"App